{"agent_id":"pp3g-hsT0-adversarial-review-of-the-b1-b6-remediation-plan-4a16","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:51:06.974798776Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"96f5e782-aa7d-43f1-9e4a-0f96e27e0954","comment_uuid":"fa3ac075-4d4b-4534-8d64-bd9024db1e2f","author":"pp3g-hsT0-adversarial-review-of-the-b1-b6-remediation-plan-4a16","content":"## Review Summary: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nIndependent adversarial review of the B1-B6 remediation plan (#361 result comment). I independently re-verified the plan's evidence claims against the repositories on disk and then attacked the plan's logic. Evidence claims: verified. Plan logic: three blocking defects (M1-M3) and seven non-blocking issues.\n\nVERIFICATION OF THE PLAN'S EVIDENCE (independently re-checked, all held):\n- Rules matrix: fork resources crosslink/rules/global.md = 9893B, Tools 10188B, ASES 10442B, tripn 10454B; project.md fork=Tools 274B vs ASES 1161B vs tripn 1.7K; knowledge.md fork=Tools 1756B vs ASES 2906B; kickoff.md ASES-only; tooling.md Tools=ASES 882B, absent from fork and tripn. ASES global.md:117 has the nohup rule; Tools' lacks it. Correct.\n- Hook logic: Tools+ASES .claude/hooks/work-check.py both use OLD (returncode==0/==2 at :291/:293); fork resources use NEW (!=2 at :292). Tools/.claude/settings.json wires exactly 6 hooks with if-[ -f ] guards. Correct.\n- Wrappers: live ~/.local/bin/claude has --agent/CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE/tmux --auto/correct \"$PROMPT\" quoting/provider list incl. opencode + memory scope; Tools/scripts/claude lacks --agent, passes --dangerously-skip-permissions through, has the ${PROMPT:+\"\"} quoting bug, provider list missing opencode. Live opencode has the #274 fork guard + REAL->...opencode.exe; Tools copy has neither. crosslink-moe identical. Correct.\n- Plugins: ASES crosslink-guard.ts 42140B / 75 agent refs / 0 hardcoded paths; tripn 37584B / 42 refs; Tools 33476B. Both repos load the 3 plugins via opencode.json. Correct.\n- Tools git: reflog proves main=be99438 is EXACTLY one commit ahead of origin/main=9fede33; uncommitted scripts/claude + global.md; .opencode/ + .worktrees/ + findings-interrupt-plugin.md untracked and NOT gitignored. Correct.\n- tripn-astro: no .ases/ dir (find = 0); EDASES-Methodology-Feedback-and-Enforcement.md §3 documents .ases/ as a design-stage integration boundary. Correct.\n- hook-config divergence: ASES encouraged/audit + by_type.builder; tripn required/enforced + git-worktree-remove gating. Correct.\n- Gitignore status of sync targets (not in the plan): .claude/hooks/ is gitignored in Tools/ASES/tripn; .opencode/plugins is NOT ignored in ASES/tripn; ~/.local/bin is not a git repo. This matters for M2/S1 below.\n\n=== MUST FIX (blocking — plan must be revised before implementation) ===\n\nM1. B4 step-5 sequence is broken against the pinned binary's actual init semantics — two failure modes, both evidenced in the fork source (~/projects/crosslink/crosslink/src/commands/init/mod.rs):\n(a) As written, 'rm -> crosslink init' does NOT redeploy hooks. Plain init on an already-initialized repo hits mod.rs:869-874 ('Already initialized — Use --force to update hooks to latest version') and returns Ok without writing anything (test test_run_already_initialized_no_force:1334 confirms). 'crosslink init --update' also refuses: deleted files are classified UpdateAction::Deleted and skipped ('deleted by user, skipping (will not recreate)', mod.rs:683-687; test_update_skips_deleted_files). So the plan's exact sequence leaves Tools agents with NO hooks — the precise bare-rm hazard B4 exists to prevent. The plan's own B4(d) scratch test would fail on the first run.\n(b) The only mode that redeploys hooks, 'crosslink init --force', is a sledgehammer: mod.rs:1045-1059 overwrites ALL of .crosslink/rules/* (RULE_FILES includes global.md/knowledge.md/project.md — test test_run_force_updates_rules proves a user-modified global.md is restored to the embedded version), and mod.rs:989 + dry-run list mod.rs:928 show it also rewrites hook-config.json, .mcp.json and .gitignore. Tools has a customized hook-config.json (2.0K) and a custom-order .mcp.json (453B vs embedded 381B) — both would be clobbered, and Tools' layer-owned global.md override (the file step 0 commits) would be silently destroyed, violating B1's entire layer-ownership protection.\nFix: specify the real mechanism. Recommended: keep the rm for D3 cleanliness but follow with 'crosslink init --force', pre-backing-up (or git-restoring from the step-0 commit) the 4 layer-owned rule files + hook-config.json + .mcp.json immediately after, and add a post-init rules-hash re-verification to both the verify step and the B4(d) scratch test. Simpler alternative: drop the rm entirely — --force rewrites the hooks in place, achieving the same end state (fresh NEW-logic hooks) with one fewer failure mode. Either way the plan must name the exact invocation and the restore set; the current text names neither. Risk register R1 covers the behavior-change risk but misses this mechanics failure.\n\nM2. B3 enforcement design is under-specified; the startup check is one-directional; the warn->hard-fail trigger is undefined.\n(a) Marker-role conflation: B3.1 says 'sync-tooling.sh writes a small manifest at each destination — Tools/plugins/.canonical-manifest.json'. Tools/plugins is the canonical SOURCE, not a destination. Two distinct artifacts are needed — a source-side canonical manifest (what '--check' compares destination files against) and a per-destination marker (what the consumer startup check compares its own file against, since 'consumers do not depend on Tools being present at runtime') — but the plan describes them as one. Marker path convention and lifecycle in destination git (tracked vs gitignored, committed vs per-sync churn vs B5's 'git status must show exactly the synced files') are unspecified.\n(b) One-directionality: the startup check (loaded file vs destination marker) detects ONLY destination-local edits. An unsynced canonical-source edit (developer edits Tools/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts and forgets to sync) is invisible at startup — consumers silently run the stale version with no banner. The plan's claim that this check 'is what makes canonical-is-Tools stick' overstates; only on-demand --check detects that direction, and its trigger ('agent preflight rule or operator's release checklist') is soft. This is a residual-drift hole in the exact D1-inversion direction the reviewers flagged.\n(c) 'warn-mode first, hard-fail after proven' — 'proven' is never operationally defined (no criterion, no flip mechanism). R8 mitigates the risk of premature hard-fail but guarantees nothing about reaching hard-fail; the risk of permanent warn-mode is real.\nFix: specify both artifacts and their locations/lifecycle; state explicitly that the startup check covers destination-side drift only and define who runs --check and when for source-side drift; define 'proven' concretely (e.g., N consecutive clean sync + --check cycles, then a tracked config flip).\n\nM3. B5's clean-worktree precondition is unsatisfiable by the plan's own step 0. B5.1 requires 'git status --porcelain must be empty in Tools and every destination'. Step 0 commits only scripts/claude + global.md, but Tools also has untracked .opencode/ (command/, package.json, .gitignore), .worktrees/, and .claude/findings-interrupt-plugin.md — none covered by Tools/.gitignore (verified). After step 0, porcelain is still non-empty, so the plan's own gate fails on the plan's own step 0.\nFix: narrow the precondition to 'no uncommitted modifications to files in the sync write-set' (untracked files outside the write-set are irrelevant to clobber safety), or extend step 0 to commit/gitignore the untracked paths.\n\n=== SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking) ===\n\nS1. B5.7 per-repo verification ('git status --porcelain must show exactly the synced files') is vacuous for gitignored and non-repo destinations: .claude/hooks/ is gitignored in Tools/ASES/tripn and ~/.local/bin is not a git repo — status shows nothing there. Make the checksum-based --check the primary acceptance gate for those paths; git status is meaningful only for tracked destinations (ASES/tripn .opencode/plugins are NOT gitignored — verified).\n\nS2. B2 tripn leg lacks a behavioral acceptance test. The ASES-functional-superset claim is grep-proven but the plugin has never been loaded under tripn's stricter hook-config (comment_discipline=required, signing_enforcement=enforced, orchestrator gates git worktree remove — verified at tripn/.crosslink/hook-config.json:186,:220,:59). WHAT-NOT-TESTED admits this, but the risk register has no compat row (R7 is drift-only). Add a scratch-repo load test with tripn's hook-config before the first real sync, and extend the B2(d) dry-run test to assert zero rules writes.\n\nS3. B3 warn-mode channel is non-durable: /tmp/crosslink-guard.log is cleared on reboot, and a 'keep enforcing' banner can scroll past. Overlaps M2(c); listed for actionability.\n\nS4. Step-0 commit of scripts/claude is dead-on-arrival: step 1 (B6) replaces the whole file with the live copy, and the plan's own sentence says the uncommitted delta 'becomes part of the canonical commit'. Commit only global.md in step 0; let step 1's replacement commit carry the wrapper delta (or stash it).\n\nS5. B5 rollback does not restore the .canonical-manifest.json markers: after --rollback, destination files are old bytes but markers record post-sync hashes, so every startup check and --check reports false drift on all rolled-back files until the next sync. Back up and restore markers alongside files.\n\nS6. B1's --include-rules opt-in scope is underdefined: a wholesale copy would recreate the exact layer-clobber hazard B1 removes. Define it to carry only the binary-distributed subset (or tooling.md), and fail loudly if a destination rule file's ownership class mismatches expectations.\n\nS7. B6/B5 deploy-leg circularity: step 1 canonicalizes FROM ~/.local/bin; step 3 deploys TO ~/.local/bin. If the live wrappers change between the two steps, step 3 silently reverts the operator's edits (no last-synced baseline exists yet). Run the deploy immediately after canonicalization, or establish the first marker baseline first.\n\n=== NOTABLE POSITIVES ===\n- Exceptionally well-grounded: every load-bearing factual claim I independently re-checked held, including details the plan didn't need to get right (exact ahead-by-1 reflog, nohup rule line numbers, plugin ref counts).\n- B1's three-class ownership model is the right abstraction and matches disk reality exactly.\n- B4's intent — pin binary, document delta, redeploy, verify, mirror in ASES — is correct; only the mechanism is broken (M1).\n- B6's 8-item contract battery is concrete and testable, and 'functional superset + repo-agnostic, not size' is the correct provenance standard.\n- WHAT-NOT-TESTED is honest and specific; the risk register is coherent, though it misses M1's mechanics.\n\n=== WHAT-NOT-TESTED (reviewer) ===\n- Could not execute crosslink init, the wrappers, or the guard plugin (read-only role; execution outside the allowed command surface). Init-behavior conclusions come from reading the fork source at its current HEAD; the plan claims the installed binary == fork HEAD 37789b51, which is consistent with the observed init-manifest/version state but was not verified at the binary level.\n- Full md5 matrix not recomputed (verified sizes for all files + content deltas for the divergent class; spot-checked the identical class).\n- Did not read reviewers #362/#364 per the independence mandate.\n- Did not exercise a live session with a drifted plugin.\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED. The plan resolves all six blockers' root causes correctly in intent and its evidence is sound, but M1 breaks the central B4 sequence against the pinned binary's actual behavior, M2 leaves B3's deliverable half-specified, and M3 is a self-contradiction between step 0 and B5. All three are cheap to fix in revision.","created_at":"2026-08-14T21:51:06.968766424Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5WECv2j12VVLbJrt4zKfPUQMsBVKcZ3b7payLcYRbEw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDXZkX2APlMC2S8MYwIB0Nmo7ixxrGmUoPRtt08OsrggAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA0fWhyQgX23+k/xQeJ8Xpu6yvuUcu7KhRE+lTaqHckPrZHV1S1f0GbS3CANrWWr+KKNzUVweNwLmPh9ofmeVpDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5WECv2j12VVLbJrt4zKfPUQMsBVKcZ3b7payLcYRbEw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDXZkX2APlMC2S8MYwIB0Nmo7ixxrGmUoPRtt08OsrggAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG1xjyY++gmPSNv8uzkB5iWGRBOQjg9VPnG3FZVpQGUpOzSbgMx++mmiwzzTnfqWUQ7oGvUaYtp8A0Pg3Jrucw4="}
